2. ELIGIBLE USERS
The User of the Software must be one of the following:
  a. An individual person, laboring for themselves.
  b. A non-profit organization.
  c. An educational institution.
  d. An organization that seeks shared profit for all of its members, and
     allows non-members to set the cost of their labor.
  e. A small commercial enterprise that employs fewer than five (5) full-time
     equivalent workers AND generates less than $100,000 USD in gross annual revenue
     in the preceding fiscal year.

For the purpose of subsection 2(e), the revenue and employee count shall be
calculated cumulatively to include the entity, its parent companies, subsidiaries,
affiliates, and any corporate group it belongs to. If the User is an organization
with owners operating under section 2(d), then all owners must be workers and all
workers must be owners with equal equity and/or equal vote.

3. RESTRICTED USERS & USES
Notwithstanding Section 2, the Software MUST NOT be used, operated, modified,
or distributed by:
  a. Law enforcement agencies, military entities, intelligence agencies, private
     security contractors working under their authority, or any entity working for,
     contracting with, or operating under the control or direction of either.
  b. Any entity or individual involved in violations of international human rights
     laws, specifically as outlined by the United Nations Universal Declaration of
     Human Rights, systematic labor exploitation, forced labor, or severe environmental
     destruction.

